     "title": "7/9 − 4/3",
     "steps": [
      "Subtracting 4/3 means adding its opposite: 7/9 − 4/3 = 7/9 + (−4/3).",
      "The denominators are 9 and 3. Their LCM is 9.",
      "9 ÷ 3 = 3, so multiply top and bottom of −4/3 by 3: (−4 × 3)/(3 × 3) = −12/9.",
      "Now add: 7/9 + (−12/9) = (7 − 12)/9.",
      "7 − 12 = −5, so the answer is −5/9."
     ],
